# Redirects for Cloudflare Pages (and Netlify), read verbatim from the deployed root.
#
# The APK is ~88 MB and Cloudflare Pages refuses any single file over 25 MiB, so the app cannot be
# hosted here. It does not need to be: it already lives on the GitHub release. This is a signpost.
#
# It points at `latest` rather than a version, and the build uploads an asset whose name never
# changes (RuneKeep-android.apk) precisely so that this line does not have to be edited on every
# release. A redirect that needs remembering is a redirect that eventually points at an old build.
#
# 302, not 301: browsers cache a permanent redirect indefinitely, and this target moves every release.

/android-app  https://github.com/DavidMGDev/RuneKeep/releases/latest/download/RuneKeep-android.apk  302
